unny oh and i  guess there's  magnus swing i think that's his name the  hot head character who allows astor to  display his true powers in anti-magic  and i guess i like him  enough characters like him are probably  better presented in anime form because  they get that vocal range to play with  and build a character through voice  alone i do however care much more about  noel i alluded to her before but she is  an interesting character  unlike astor who was a poor lad willing  to accept whatever came his way  noel is a lady of nobility great things  were expected of her but she had to  settle for the worst squad because they  turned out to be the only ones that  would take her so another great  dichotomy here between noel and astor  and i especially like the scene near the  end of the first arc where the two of  them were discussing money and it's just  so clear that noel doesn't understand  the value of money despite being  absolutely loaded with it meanwhile  asta's like well with this tiny amount i  could do this  this and this there's also a stark  contrast with magic of course  as a member of fine nobility noel is  well responsible for i think the  greatest magic power i've seen depicted  so far and her problem is she can't  control it which is something i greatly  enjoy  characters without flaws are incredibly  boring and noel's flaw is in perfect  balance to her  talent all the power in the world but  completely incapable of wielding it  properly that works for me and i guess  it works as a final counter to astor as  well because noel seems to be something  of an epitome of magic whilst asta is  the epitome of i guess  anti-magic it's very similar to the  aster unidynamic actually and i'm  wondering if noel and yuna might flip  roles in the future you know yuno  becomes corrupted by nobility resources  and power  and stuff whilst noel learns to be far  more humbled and appreciate the smaller  things in life  maybe maybe not maybe i shouldn't even  be trying t