d by his random  appearance  i personally come from the one piece  school of thinking that i like  keeping key figures in the shadows for  long periods of time before an eventual  revelation but in black clover we've now  already revealed the ultimate wizard bro  as well as seeing quite a few of the  squad captains during the entrance exam  like yami william like we saw at least  seven of them  possibly more and i'm just like slow  down  build your house up one brick at a time  save these guys for something more  dramatic because now that we've seen the  wizard king that's great we have a roof  for our house but we don't have any  walls to hold it up that might just be a  me thing though a lot of  things and me things in any case that's  our introduction to black clover it's a  series that really could go one of two  ways to me  either it could exceed all expectations  and develop into an above average shonen  journey which is what i'm hoping for  however it could also land in a very  middling to mediocre place the  genericism does worry me quite a bit but  at the same time you really can't judge  a shonen series by the first handful of  chapters so if you'd like to see me keep  going  you know the thing that it is you need  to do but that pretty much does it for  this blind review of black clover's  introductory arc and what do you guys  think please do leave your thoughts in  the comments below or even join my  discord server and don't forget to  subscribe to the channel for very  maybe black clover goodness delivered  straight into your youtube feed but for  now this has been the new world review  and i'll see you next time

